  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Mozambique 2023 &#x2013; Urban planner or resilience II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In February 2023, Mozambique suffered from heavy and persistent rains due to the passage of cyclone Freddy. Due to strong winds and ongoing heavy rainfall, there was an above normal flow in the river basin throughout the country, isolating several districts, especially in the central region. This resulted in deaths, displacements and the destruction of socio-economic infrastructure, worsening the already critical humanitarian situation in-country.Mozambique has requested technical assistance through the DRRS programme. The aim is to reduce the risk of natural disasters caused by water through the definition of short-, medium- and long-term prevention and mitigation measures. This will be done by demonstrating the added value of an inclusive integrated approach by organising a collaboration workshop with local authorities, funding organisations and diverse stakeholders, stressing the wider context of cyclone or flood threat in Mozambique and emphasising the importance of sustainably achieving resilience for cities, communities, economies and ecologies.The urban planner or resilience expert will prepare and support the 3-day &quot;Mozambican-Dutch dialogues&quot; workshop with conceptual designs for integrated solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
